---
title: Chili Mac Rice Cakes
description: Chewy rice cakes take the macaroni's place in this one-skillet chili mac with beef and cheddar.
tags: [one-pan]
course: main
icons: [pepper-hot, cheese, pan-frying]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Food52
  url: https://food52.com/recipes/87249-best-chili-mac-rice-cakes-recipe
servings: 4
prep time: 10m
cook time: 15m
---

If working with frozen rice cakes, place them in a #medium bowl{}. Cover with cold water and thaw for about ~thaw{10%minutes} while proceeding with the recipe, then drain. If working with room-temperature rice cakes, skip this step.

In a large, heavy-bottomed #skillet{}, heat the @neutral oil{1%tbsp} over medium-high heat. Add the @ground beef{1%lb}(16 oz, 80/20 preferred), the @kosher salt{1%tsp}, and the @black pepper{1/4%tsp}(freshly ground, plus more as needed). Break up the meat and cook until the pink is gone, about ~cook{4-5%minutes}.

Add the @yellow onion{1}(medium, chopped) and @garlic cloves{4-5}(minced) and cook until the onion is translucent, another few minutes.

Lower the heat to medium. Add the @sweet or smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @chili powder{1%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}, @tomato paste{1/4%cup}, and @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp}. Stir and combine with the meat and onion mixture. (Lower the heat a touch more if you see the tomato paste is sticking to the bottom of the skillet.)

Add the @whole milk{1%cup} and @water{1%cup} and stir everything carefully, scraping up any bits on the bottom of the pan.

Add the @cylinder-shaped rice cakes{510-567%g}(18 to 20 oz) to the skillet, breaking any stuck-together ones apart. They should be about halfway submerged; don't worry if they're not fully covered by the liquid.

Turn the heat back up to medium-high, and cook until the rice cakes are done but still chewy and al dente, about ~cook{4-5%minutes}. If they were particularly hard or dry to begin with, it might take a few more minutes. (They will continue getting softer with residual heat, so err on cooking for a shorter time rather than longer.) Keep an eye on the skillet and reduce the heat if the sauce starts to bubble aggressively or splatter. Stir once in a while to prevent the rice cakes from sticking to the pan.

Turn off the heat and add the @extra sharp cheddar{227%g}(8 oz, 2 cups, white or yellow, grated). Carefully stir until combined and all the cheese is melted. The sauce will thicken further at this point. Taste and adjust the seasoning, adding the last @&kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, if needed.

Plate and garnish with the @scallion{1}(thinly sliced) and extra freshly cracked black pepper. Enjoy right away.
